ask.status = \"skipped\"` and `task.error = \"upstream failure\"`; otherwise invoke `self.handlers[name]()`, recording `task.result` and `task.status = \"succeeded\"`, or catching `Exception as exc` to set `task.status = \"failed\"` and `task.error = str(exc)`.\n  - Return `{name: self.graph.tasks[name].status for name in order}`.\n\n### Verify Command\n- `python -m pytest -q --tb=short` (or `pytest -q --tb=short` if `pytest` is on PATH)\n","duration_seconds":9.0465961,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":26097,"output_tokens":1199,"thinking_tokens":114,"cache_read_tokens":24008,"total_tokens":27296}}}
